              "name": "Sankey - Material Flow",
              "style": {
                "classes": ""
              },
              "viewParams": {
                "_description": "Material flow down the Alarm Flood line as a Sankey diagram. Each station emits two bands: what it passes downstream and what it is accumulating in its own buffer. On a healthy line the chain runs full width and the held bands are hairlines; during a jam the held bands fatten from the downstream end backwards, so the whole cascade reads in one frame. Best single widget for \u0027where is the line backing up\u0027. Values are % of each station\u0027s nominal rate, not units/min. linePath (string, optional) - Alarm Flood line path, e.g. \"Site1/Area1/Line1\". Leave empty to follow the simulator\u0027s default line, which is what the Alarm Flood Event page drives.",
                "_generated": "canvas-charts (generated by scripts/gen_dashboard_widgets.py)",
                "footer": "",
                "header": "",
                "linePath": ""
              },
              "viewPath": "Exchange/Dashboard Agent/Dashboard Templates/sankey"
